<h2 id="about-the-emacs-cat">About The Emacs Cat</h2>
<p>My first attempt to dive into the vast ocean of Emacs was in 1997,
over 25 years ago.</p>
<p>My first attempt was unsuccessful; I now realize I couldn’t fully
grasp the spirit of Emacs at the time.</p>
<p>My second—and successful—attempt came in 2012. Since then, I’ve been
using Emacs for nearly everything, from coding in <a href="https://olddeuteronomy.github.io/post/cpp-programming-in-emacs/">C++</a>
and <a href="https://olddeuteronomy.github.io/post/python-programming-in-emacs/">Python</a> to
maintaining my knowledge base with <em>org-roam</em> and writing articles in <em>LaTeX</em>.</p>